{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-99286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-99286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{1}-2{e}^{0},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2e-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-99286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2963be037eece84c10fba127787e4615316af37cfca85c49b4183a13349ba51c"} {"question" "q-99286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-99286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2e-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2{e}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2⟩"] ["math" "⟨e-2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡1⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{2}+1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{2}-e,\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-99286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2e-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int {e}^{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)={e}^{t+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t+1}\\text{d}t={e}^{t+1}+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=3t.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{e}^{t+1}+{c}_{1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2963be037eece84c10fba127787e4615316af37cfca85c49b4183a13349ba51c"} {"question" "q-123435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨{e}^{3t},\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{t-1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\int ⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {e}^{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=\\frac{t}{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 4\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)={e}^{t-1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t-1}\\text{d}t={e}^{t-1}+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{t-1}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2963be037eece84c10fba127787e4615316af37cfca85c49b4183a13349ba51c"} {"question" "q-123438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C"] ["math" "⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t),\\,(t-1){e}^{t-1}⟩+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-123438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component, let $u=2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$, so $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second component, we integrate directly:\n\n$$\n\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t){|}_{0}^{\\pi /3},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3),\\,-4\\,(\\frac{1}{2}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ln\\,(\\frac{4}{3}),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ln\\,(\\frac{4}{3}),\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2963be037eece84c10fba127787e4615316af37cfca85c49b4183a13349ba51c"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{4}{3})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349111" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨2{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(0)=⟨1,\\,-4⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨2{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨2{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 2{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 6{t}^{2}-2\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{-t}+{c}_{1},\\,2{t}^{3}-2t+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨1,\\,-4⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨-2{e}^{0}+{c}_{1},\\,2(0)^{3}-2(0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,-4⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2+{c}_{1},\\,0+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=3$ and ${c}_{2}=-4.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨-2{e}^{-t}+3,\\,2{t}^{3}-2t-4⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2963be037eece84c10fba127787e4615316af37cfca85c49b4183a13349ba51c"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2e^{-t}+3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"} {"question" "q-349375" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t^3-2t-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064221/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f371bb3e6dbc59ee64b87ebc0f7a0cbd54d718f47f4d6ed744177e5a4466be7"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2095 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
